---
import WebsiteShowcase
  from "../components/case-study/WebsiteShowcase.astro";

import type {
  Project,
} from "../data/projects";


interface Props {
  project: Project;
}

const {
  project,
} = Astro.props;
---

<!-- =======================================================
     FMIPA PROJECT OPENING
     Editorial / web-design language
     ======================================================= -->

<section
  class="site-container pt-10 md:pt-16"
>
  <div
    class="grid gap-12 pb-12 md:grid-cols-12 md:pb-16"
  >
    <!-- Main identity -->

    <div
      class="md:col-span-8"
    >
      <p
        class="rule-label text-accent"
      >
        Institutional Website / 2026
      </p>

      <h1
        class="mt-10 max-w-[1100px] text-[clamp(3.8rem,7.5vw,8.5rem)] leading-[0.88] font-medium tracking-[-0.06em]"
      >
        FMIPA UGM
        <span
          class="editorial-serif"
        >
          Website Redesign.
        </span>
      </h1>
    </div>


    <!-- Metadata -->

    <aside
      class="flex flex-col justify-end gap-8 border-t border-line pt-6 md:col-span-3 md:col-start-10 md:border-t-0 md:border-l md:pt-0 md:pl-8"
    >
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted"
        >
          Role
        </p>

        <p
          class="mt-2 text-[14px] leading-[1.6]"
        >
          UI/UX Designer
          <br />
          Frontend contributor
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p
          class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted"
        >
          Scope
        </p>

        <p
          class="mt-2 text-[14px] leading-[1.6]"
        >
          Information architecture
          <br />
          Visual system
          <br />
          WordPress implementation
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p
          class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted"
        >
          Year
        </p>

        <p
          class="mt-2 text-[14px]"
        >
          {project.year}
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>


  <!-- Main website image -->

  <figure
    class="border-y border-ink py-5 md:py-7"
  >
    <div
      class="relative aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden bg-panel"
    >
      <img
        src="/images/projects/fmipa/new-home.png"
        alt="Redesigned FMIPA UGM faculty homepage"
        class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-top"
      />
    </div>

    <figcaption
      class="grid gap-4 pt-4 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.07em] text-muted md:grid-cols-3"
    >
      <p>
        Faculty homepage
      </p>

      <p class="md:text-center">
        Figma → WordPress
      </p>

      <p class="md:text-right">
        FMIPA Universitas Gadjah Mada
      </p>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>


  <!-- Opening statement -->

  <div
    class="grid gap-8 py-14 md:grid-cols-12 md:py-20"
  >
    <div
      class="md:col-span-3"
    >
      <p
        class="rule-label text-muted"
      >
        The brief
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="md:col-span-8 md:col-start-5"
    >
      <p
        class="max-w-[980px] text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,4.6rem)] leading-[1.04] font-medium tracking-[-0.04em]"
      >
        The project was not simply about giving the
        faculty website a newer look. It meant
        deciding what information belonged together,
        what could disappear, and how one design
        system could support very different
        <span
          class="editorial-serif"
        >
          kinds of academic content.
        </span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =======================================================
     01 / DIAGNOSIS
     ======================================================= -->

<section
  class="site-container py-20 md:py-32"
>
  <div
    class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div
      class="md:col-span-3"
    >
      <p
        class="rule-label text-muted"
      >
        01 / Why redesign
      </p>
    </div>


    <div
      class="md:col-span-8 md:col-start-5"
    >
      <h2
        class="max-w-[950px] text-[clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5.8rem)] leading-[0.98] font-medium tracking-[-0.05em]"
      >
        A visual refresh would have solved
        <span
          class="editorial-serif"
        >
          the least important problem.
        </span>
      </h2>


      <p
        class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-muted md:text-[16px]"
      >
        The previous faculty website had accumulated
        problems across both presentation and
        structure. Content had grown over time,
        destinations overlapped, responsive behaviour
        was limited, and parts of the interface
        depended on assets that were increasingly
        difficult to maintain.
      </p>


      <!-- Issues -->

      <div
        class="mt-16 border-t border-ink"
      >

        <div
          class="grid gap-5 border-b border-line py-7 md:grid-cols-12 md:py-9"
        >
          <p
            class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-accent md:col-span-1"
          >
            01
          </p>

          <h3
            class="text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.2vw,2.4rem)] leading-[1.08] font-medium tracking-[-0.035em] md:col-span-5"
          >
            Navigation had become fragmented.
          </h3>

          <p
            class="max-w-lg text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-muted md:col-span-6"
          >
            Important information was distributed
            across many destinations, while several
            pages overlapped in purpose or were
            difficult to discover.
          </p>
        </div>


        <div
          class="grid gap-5 border-b border-line py-7 md:grid-cols-12 md:py-9"
        >
          <p
            class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-accent md:col-span-1"
          >
            02
          </p>

          <h3
            class="text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.2vw,2.4rem)] leading-[1.08] font-medium tracking-[-0.035em] md:col-span-5"
          >
            The interface no longer felt coherent.
          </h3>

          <p
            class="max-w-lg text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-muted md:col-span-6"
          >
            Visual hierarchy, component behaviour,
            responsive treatment, and long-form
            content presentation had become
            inconsistent across the website.
          </p>
        </div>


        <div
          class="grid gap-5 border-b border-line py-7 md:grid-cols-12 md:py-9"
        >
          <p
            class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-accent md:col-span-1"
          >
            03
          </p>

          <h3
            class="text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.2vw,2.4rem)] leading-[1.08] font-medium tracking-[-0.035em] md:col-span-5"
          >
            Maintenance mattered too.
          </h3>

          <p
            class="max-w-lg text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-muted md:col-span-6"
          >
            Some existing components relied on paid
            assets and tooling, so the redesign also
            needed to leave the faculty with a system
            that was practical to maintain.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =======================================================
     BEFORE / AFTER
     ======================================================= -->

<section
  class="site-container pb-24 md:pb-40"
>
  <div
    class="border-t border-ink pt-5"
  >
    <div
      class="mb-8 flex items-center justify-between"
    >
      <p
        class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted"
      >
        Before / After
      </p>

      <p
        class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted"
      >
        About FMIPA
      </p>
    </div>


    <div
      class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2"
    >

      <!-- Previous -->

      <figure>
        <div
          class="relative aspect-[16/11] overflow-hidden bg-panel"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/projects/fmipa/old-about.png"
            alt="Previous FMIPA UGM About page"
            loading="lazy"
            class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-top"
          />
        </div>

        <figcaption
          class="grid gap-4 border-t border-line pt-4 md:grid-cols-3"
        >
          <p
            class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em]"
          >
            Before
          </p>

          <p
            class="text-[12px] leading-[1.65] text-muted md:col-span-2"
          >
            Dense long-form content, weaker visual
            grouping, and an older interface system.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>


      <!-- Redesigned -->

      <figure>
        <div
          class="relative aspect-[16/11] overflow-hidden bg-panel"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/projects/fmipa/new-about.png"
            alt="Redesigned FMIPA UGM About page"
            loading="lazy"
            class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-top"
          />
        </div>

        <figcaption
          class="grid gap-4 border-t border-line pt-4 md:grid-cols-3"
        >
          <p
            class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-accent"
          >
            Redesigned
          </p>

          <p
            class="text-[12px] leading-[1.65] text-muted md:col-span-2"
          >
            Stronger hierarchy, clearer information
            grouping, and one visual language carried
            across long-form content.
          </p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =======================================================
     02 / INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE
     ======================================================= -->

<section
  class="bg-ink text-paper"
>
  <div
    class="site-container py-20 md:py-32 lg:py-40"
  >
    <div
      class="grid gap-14 md:grid-cols-12"
    >
      <div
        class="md:col-span-3"
      >
        <p
          class="rule-label text-accent"
        >
          02 / Structure first
        </p>
      </div>


      <div
        class="md:col-span-8 md:col-start-5"
      >
        <h2
          class="max-w-[960px] text-[clamp(2.8rem,5.6vw,6.2rem)] leading-[0.96] font-medium tracking-[-0.055em]"
        >
          Before drawing pages, I reduced
          what the website asked people
          <span
            class="editorial-serif"
          >
            to navigate.
          </span>
        </h2>

        <p
          class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-paper/55"
        >
          Instead of reproducing the existing site
          structure inside a newer interface, related
          information was consolidated into clearer
          destinations and the page hierarchy was
          reconsidered before high-fidelity design.
        </p>


        <div
          class="mt-16 border-t border-paper/25"
        >

          <div
            class="grid gap-6 border-b border-paper/15 py-8 md:grid-cols-12"
          >
            <p
              class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.08em] text-paper/40 md:col-span-1"
            >
              01
            </p>

            <h3
              class="text-xl font-medium tracking-[-0.025em] md:col-span-4"
            >
              Consolidate
            </h3>

            <p
              class="max-w-xl text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-paper/55 md:col-span-7"
            >
              Overlapping and redundant destinations
              were brought together rather than
              carried forward simply because they
              already existed.
            </p>
          </div>


          <div
            class="grid gap-6 border-b border-paper/15 py-8 md:grid-cols-12"
          >
            <p
              class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.08em] text-paper/40 md:col-span-1"
            >
              02
            </p>

            <h3
              class="text-xl font-medium tracking-[-0.025em] md:col-span-4"
            >
              Re-prioritize
            </h3>

            <p
              class="max-w-xl text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-paper/55 md:col-span-7"
            >
              Navigation and page structure were
              organized around what visitors needed
              to find, rather than around the history
              of how the old website had grown.
            </p>
          </div>


          <div
            class="grid gap-6 border-b border-paper/15 py-8 md:grid-cols-12"
          >
            <p
              class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.08em] text-paper/40 md:col-span-1"
            >
              03
            </p>

            <h3
              class="text-xl font-medium tracking-[-0.025em] md:col-span-4"
            >
              Build a shared system
            </h3>

            <p
              class="max-w-xl text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-paper/55 md:col-span-7"
            >
              Very different content types still
              needed to feel like one faculty website,
              so typography, navigation, spacing, and
              reusable interface behaviour became the
              common layer.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>


        <!-- Team -->

        <div
          class="mt-16 grid gap-8 border-t border-paper/25 pt-8 md:grid-cols-2"
        >
          <div>
            <p
              class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-paper/40"
            >
              Design responsibility
            </p>

            <p
              class="mt-4 max-w-md text-[14px] leading-[1.7] text-paper/70"
            >
              I was the project's sole UI/UX designer,
              responsible for the visual direction,
              information architecture, page flow,
              layout decisions, component direction,
              and image selection.
            </p>
          </div>


          <div>
            <p
              class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-paper/40"
            >
              Development structure
            </p>

            <p
              class="mt-4 max-w-md text-[14px] leading-[1.7] text-paper/70"
            >
              Development was handled by a two-person
              team. I contributed primarily on the
              frontend while another developer handled
              more of the backend and custom
              functionality.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- =======================================================
     03 / VISUAL DIRECTION
     ======================================================= -->

<section
  class="site-container py-24 md:py-40"
>
  <div
    class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div
      class="md:col-span-3"
    >
      <p
        class="rule-label text-muted"
      >
        03 / Direction
      </p>
    </div>


    <div
      class="md:col-span-8 md:col-start-5"
    >
      <h2
        class="max-w-[900px] text-[clamp(2.7rem,5vw,5.8rem)] leading-[0.98] font-medium tracking-[-0.05em]"
      >
        Contemporary, but still recognizably
        <span
          class="editorial-serif"
        >
          FMIPA UGM.
        </span>
      </h2>

      <div
        class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2"
      >
        <p
          class="text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-muted"
        >
          Early exploration drew from university
          websites whose editorial structure felt
          appropriate for the direction being
          discussed with the team. A Japanese
          university website became the strongest
          shared visual reference.
        </p>

        <p
          class="text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-muted"
        >
          The reference was never treated as a
          template. Its qualities were translated
          into a system that still respected UGM's
          existing colours, institutional marks,
          content requirements, and technical
          environment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>


  <!-- Exploration images -->

  <div
    class="mt-16 grid items-start gap-5 md:mt-24 md:grid-cols-12"
  >

    <figure
      class="md:col-span-5"
    >
      <div
        class="overflow-hidden bg-[#1d1d1d]"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/projects/fmipa/figma-exploration.png"
          alt="Early FMIPA website design exploration in Figma"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block h-auto w-full"
        />
      </div>

      <figcaption
        class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-5 border-t border-line pt-3"
      >
        <span
          class="text-[10px] text-accent"
        >
          A
        </span>

        <p
          class="text-[11px] leading-[1.65] text-muted"
        >
          An earlier direction that was explored and
          later discarded.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>


    <figure
      class="md:col-span-7 md:mt-24"
    >
      <div
        class="overflow-hidden bg-[#1d1d1d]"
      >
        <img
          src="/images/projects/fmipa/figma-overview.png"
          alt="High-fidelity FMIPA website designs in Figma"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block h-auto w-full"
        />
      </div>

      <figcaption
        class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-5 border-t border-line pt-3"
      >
        <span
          class="text-[10px] text-accent"
        >
          B
        </span>

        <p
          class="text-[11px] leading-[1.65] text-muted"
        >
          High-fidelity development of the visual
          system across several page types.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- =======================================================
     04 / FINAL SYSTEM
     ======================================================= -->

<section
  class="site-container pt-12 md:pt-20"
>
  <div
    class="grid gap-12 border-t border-ink pt-10 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div
      class="md:col-span-3"
    >
      <p
        class="rule-label text-muted"
      >
        04 / The system
      </p>
    </div>


    <div
      class="md:col-span-8 md:col-start-5"
    >
      <h2
        class="max-w-[960px] text-[clamp(2.7rem,5vw,5.8rem)] leading-[0.98] font-medium tracking-[-0.05em]"
      >
        One identity, applied to pages with
        <span
          class="editorial-serif"
        >
          very different jobs.
        </span>
      </h2>

      <p
        class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-muted"
      >
        Shared typography, spacing, navigation,
        components, colours, and interaction patterns
        create continuity. Individual pages are still
        allowed to respond to their own content,
        audience, and purpose.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<WebsiteShowcase
  src="/images/projects/fmipa/new-home.png"
  alt="Redesigned FMIPA UGM homepage"
  number="04.1"
  title="Faculty Homepage"
  description="The central entry point brings departments, admissions, faculty information, news, academic updates, and events into one navigable overview."
  tone="warm"
  previewPosition="top"
/>

<WebsiteShowcase
  src="/images/projects/fmipa/new-about.png"
  alt="Redesigned FMIPA UGM About page"
  number="04.2"
  title="About FMIPA"
  description="A long-form institutional page combining faculty overview, statistics, history, academics, strategy, governance, and organizational information."
  tone="paper"
  previewPosition="top"
/>

<WebsiteShowcase
  src="/images/projects/fmipa/new-iup.png"
  alt="Redesigned FMIPA UGM International Undergraduate Program page"
  number="04.3"
  title="International Undergraduate Program"
  description="A recruitment-oriented page structured around program value, international exposure, study pathways, student support, available programs, and tuition."
  tone="blue"
  previewPosition="top"
/>

<!-- =======================================================
     05 / IMPLEMENTATION
     ======================================================= -->

<section
  class="site-container py-24 md:py-40"
>
  <div
    class="grid gap-12 border-t border-ink pt-10 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <div
      class="md:col-span-3"
    >
      <p
        class="rule-label text-muted"
      >
        05 / Implementation
      </p>
    </div>


    <div
      class="md:col-span-8 md:col-start-5"
    >
      <h2
        class="max-w-[900px] text-[clamp(2.6rem,5vw,5.8rem)] leading-[0.98] font-medium tracking-[-0.05em]"
      >
        The design still had to survive
        <span
          class="editorial-serif"
        >
          WordPress.
        </span>
      </h2>

      <p
        class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-muted"
      >
        Implementation added constraints that were
        largely invisible inside Figma. The website
        needed to work with the faculty's existing
        environment and rely on free WordPress tooling
        rather than premium dependencies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>


  <!-- Three implementation dimensions -->

  <div
    class="mt-16 grid border-y border-ink md:grid-cols-3"
  >

    <article
      class="border-b border-line py-8 md:border-r md:border-b-0 md:px-8 md:first:pl-0"
    >
      <p
        class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-accent"
      >
        Constraint
      </p>

      <h3
        class="mt-5 text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.035em]"
      >
        Free tooling
      </h3>

      <p
        class="mt-5 max-w-sm text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-muted"
      >
        The implementation relied on free WordPress
        plugins, including Elementor Basic rather
        than Elementor Pro.
      </p>
    </article>


    <article
      class="border-b border-line py-8 md:border-r md:border-b-0 md:px-8"
    >
      <p
        class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-accent"
      >
        Contribution
      </p>

      <h3
        class="mt-5 text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.035em]"
      >
        Frontend implementation
      </h3>

      <p
        class="mt-5 max-w-sm text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-muted"
      >
        I contributed to frontend implementation
        and personally implemented the Organization
        Structure experience, including lecturer
        profile information.
      </p>
    </article>


    <article
      class="py-8 md:px-8 md:last:pr-0"
    >
      <p
        class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-accent"
      >
        Validation
      </p>

      <h3
        class="mt-5 text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.035em]"
      >
        Three UAT rounds
      </h3>

      <p
        class="mt-5 max-w-sm text-[14px] leading-[1.75] text-muted"
      >
        Lecturers and faculty leadership reviewed the
        website through three rounds of User
        Acceptance Testing.
      </p>
    </article>

  </div>


  <!-- UAT outcome -->

  <div
    class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-12"
  >
    <p
      class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted md:col-span-3"
    >
      What changed after testing
    </p>

    <p
      class="max-w-3xl text-[clamp(1.4rem,2.5vw,2.7rem)] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.03em] md:col-span-8 md:col-start-5"
    >
      The core design direction remained largely
      intact. Feedback focused mostly on smaller
      functional adjustments, editorial corrections,
      and content revisions.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

